From 7e58c9395e538e5e787156cc39035f5865ec2e89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baKon <mike.ski83@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:52:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] format: a span per stacked part, and a share that is
 zeros

Two additive builder exports, RAD_ABI_VERSION untouched.

rad_weight_shard_span_parts: a row-sharded weight whose stacked parts
are not the same width -- the delta net's [q|k|v|z], 2048, 2048, 6144,
6144 rows on Flash-Next -- cannot take rad_weight_shard_span's one
[lo, hi), which is applied to every part and assumes them equal. This
takes a span per part together with each part's whole extent in the
container; share.cpp cuts every part by its own rows and refuses totals
that do not sum to the entry. It is how a rank declares an UNEVEN share
of the heads -- 6 of 16 K heads where three ranks take 6, 5 and 5 --
with nothing padded.

rad_weight_shard_zero: this rank's share of a row- or column-sharded
weight is zeros. weight_share returns the declaration's extents with no
rectangles; the loader stages the weight with a worker that writes
zeros (the route a checkpoint weight already takes from a container)
and reads nothing. It is for a rank the geometry gives no real heads
(next commit), which then declares the same program as its peers.

share_test holds the per-part cut and the zero share.
