From: baKon <mike.ski83@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:42:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] load: a zero share is delivered from a container, and
 an undelivered slot refuses

From a container the relayout workers are fed by the sweep over the file, and a
zero share (rad_weight_shard_zero: an attention-zero rank's q|gate, k, v and o)
has no bytes in the file, so nothing ever arrived for it, its worker never ran,
and its slot held whatever the card had there. On a card whose freed VRAM the
driver wipes that is zeros and the rank serves correctly by luck; on a card
fresh from a reset ("VRAM is lost") it is garbage and every token is garbage.
The checkpoint branch hands every staged weight to the workers itself, which is
why the hole was never seen there.

Zero shares are now handed to the workers before the sweep, and the pool's
finish() refuses when any staged weight was never delivered, so a slot nothing
wrote cannot serve again.

Reproducer on any card: RADIANCE_POISON_ALLOC=255 with an odd world over a
container (--tp 3 on a two-KV-head model).
---
 core/engine_bringup.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/engine_bringup.cpp b/core/engine_bringup.cpp
index 50f74b3..bf2c9b6 100644
--- a/core/engine_bringup.cpp
+++ b/core/engine_bringup.cpp
@@ -1388,6 +1388,27 @@ public:
