From 7612f9de1b9350da2b9029428cf99613cbb61304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baKon <mike.ski83@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:12:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] libr4d: a fill op

y = value over an [M, n] extent at a row pitch, bf16, default 0. The op a rank
issues where it has nothing to compute and a reader downstream -- an all-reduce,
a residual -- still expects a defined buffer: a wire shared across layers cannot
be zeroed once a step, and a memset knows neither the pitch nor the dtype.
Smoke-tested for the exact zero, the pitch, and the RNE of a value.
---
 libr4d/r4d.h              |  1 +
 libr4d/r4d_model_bf16.hip | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libr4d/r4d_plugin.h       |  2 ++
 libr4d/r4d_rows.cpp       | 20 ++++++++++++++++++
