the scheduler indexes groups by position and one block table serves every
rank -- and this rank carves nothing for it: its block count is the shared
table's, its costs are zero, its pool base is null, and issue refuses any op
on this rank that names it. For a rank the geometry gives no attention heads,
whose attention is a fill of zeros and never stores or reads a key. qwen4exp
declares its attention group so on such a rank. The arch test's contract
becomes the real one: same KV groups by position; ops are each rank's own.
