From 31c429ec3334f265524246f0b1bb96a534b847a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baKon <mike.ski83@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:33:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] Revert "budget: a rank whose cache costs less backs the
 same tokens with a smaller pool"

This reverts commit fa01bd2. Its premise -- the attention-zero rank holds
a larger share of the experts, so the bytes its cache does not need are
best spent in its weights pool -- went with the experts' remainder-first
placement (665d181): the experts cut as every world always has and no
rank has a larger share. What the re-split did keep was a KV pool on that
rank a third the size of its peers', and BetterBench after three 250k
prefills (a cache three quarters full) decoded 13-23% slower at every
concurrency than the same tree without it, while a cold server measured
faster. The pool goes back to the common split; what the rank does not
carve for attention it lends, as every rank's idle cache does.
